<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Semiramis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shamiram</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Semiramis is a legendary queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> in Greek tradition, credited with founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, building great works and leading campaigns as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The legend probably drew on Shammuramat, the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adad-nirari-iii">Adad-nirari III</a>, who was influential at the Assyrian court around 800 BCE. In Armenian tradition, as Shamiram, she desired the hero Ara the Handsome, and Urartian works around Van, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menua">Menua</a>'s canal, were attributed to her.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/semiramis.jpg" alt="Semiramis" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Smerdis of Tlön · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Semiramis-Regina.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
